# Cursor Rules for OkeApp (Next.js, Supabase, Vercel, GitHub)

## Coding & Architecture
- Use **TypeScript** with strict typing. Avoid `any`.
- Keep component sizes small and focused.
- Use **Vanilla CSS** for core layouts/components as preferred in this project (defined in [globals.css](file:///C:/xampp/htdocs/karaoke/app/globals.css)).
- For interactive features like the video player, room state, or song queue, use **Client Components** (`"use client"`).

## Next.js (App Router)
- Group pages in `app/`.
- Handle backend logic/YouTube API proxy requests inside API Routes (`app/api/`).
- Follow the rules in [AGENTS.md](file:///C:/xampp/htdocs/karaoke/AGENTS.md) carefully for breaking changes in Next.js versions.

## Supabase
- Use Supabase Realtime for instant queue and player sync.
- Keep migration scripts updated in [migration.sql](file:///C:/xampp/htdocs/karaoke/supabase/migration.sql).
- Secure tables using Row Level Security (RLS).

## Vercel & Deployment
- Ensure environment variables (`NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`, `YOUTUBE_API_KEY`) are set correctly.
- Test build locally via `npm run build` before pushing.

## GitHub Workflow
- Write clean and descriptive commit messages following Conventional Commits (e.g., `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `style:`).
